      "writtenOn": "2020-11-18T04:56:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The crash definitely looks like it\u0027s inside __schedule for reasons stated on the bug. `tasks` is static so we don\u0027t get a symbol out, but the constraint for hitting the crash is actually if `(uint8_t)(current_task - tasks)` \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_CONSOLE since task_id_t is fixed to 8 bits wide.\n\nInspecting symbols at a8dec10c9da00eca5284ee34246fdeadf1ba9179 (where the crash is reproducible), scratchpad (the initial value for current_task) is at 200b1e84 and tasks appears to be at 200b0590. Taking the exact sequence of operations from the disassembly of task_get_current:\n\n    \u003e\u003e\u003e scratchpad \u003d 0x200b1e84\n    \u003e\u003e\u003e tasks \u003d 0x200b0590\n    \u003e\u003e\u003e (((scratchpad - tasks) \u003e\u003e 3) * 0xAAAAAAAB) \u0026 0xFF\n    10\n\n[It turns out that naively dividing the raw pointer difference by 24 (the post-alignment size of the task_ struct) yields a different result, so it\u0027s important to do the same multiply-by-reciprocal operation as the compiler synthesizes to do the division by 24!]",
      "parentUuid": "71f7a2e4_c4f2ca36",
